"""Graduated topic hints and additional assessor discriminators for subtle cases."""
HINTS={
'T07.01':('Name the last stage that reads a header.','Compare the frozen preprocessed text before investigating assembler or linker inputs.'),
'T07.02':('Classify the machine that runs each tool separately from the machine described by its output.','Compare driver target and selected search roots with the produced object attributes.'),
'T07.03':('Separate a required language diagnostic from an optional warning policy.','Use a valid control and an out-of-scope warning to test both the runner and suppression boundary.'),
'T07.04':('Keep semantic inputs fixed while changing one build profile.','Inspect effective commands and final dependencies, not only preset names or intermediate objects.'),
'T07.05':('Draw each produced file and the exact bytes needed to produce it.','Distinguish the edge needed for creation order from the edge that should invalidate an existing output.'),
'T07.06':('Write the consumer compile requirements before deciding visibility keywords.','A static archive may still require implementation libraries when the final executable links.'),
'T07.07':('Identify whether the missing input is needed during configuration or build.','Delete a generated output and observe whether its producer is actually reachable in the graph.'),
'T07.08':('Identify the selected configuration and output before replaying a database row.','The working directory resolves relative paths; generated inputs and the final link still need separate records.'),
'T07.09':('List target libraries separately from executable host utilities.','Compare the resolved path and ABI attributes before interpreting a successful compiler invocation.'),
'T07.10':('Distinguish the dependency label from the bytes that were verified.','Test a missing transitive input in the local cache; a previous populated cache can hide an undeclared dependency.'),
'T07.11':('A test verdict needs an execution scope and a failure cause.','Require a same-toolchain positive control before interpreting a negative case as the intended rejection.'),
'T07.12':('Separate behavior, selected section bytes and whole-file identity.','Check path/time/generated metadata before applying normalization, and preserve the unnormalized provenance.'),
'T08.01':('Annotate operand widths and effective addresses before predicting the value.','Apply the actual structure stride and member offset; instruction meaning alone supplies no timing model.'),
'T08.02':('List state owned by caller and callee before evaluating the numeric answer.','Use independent sentinel values and distinguish carry/overflow from signed/unsigned branch selection.'),
'T08.03':('Classify each eightbyte before assigning available register classes.','Account for the call-pushed return address and a hidden result pointer before locating later arguments.'),
'T08.04':('Distinguish a logical activation from an observed machine frame.','Look for live values across calls and data below rsp before claiming a stack bound.'),
'T08.05':('Measure widths, offsets and alignments independently.','An object linker usually sees symbols, not both translation units\' complete C type layouts.'),
'T08.06':('Separate instructions used inside the function from registers used at its boundary.','Check VFP argument candidates and preserved-register rules under the exact AAPCS variant.'),
'T08.07':('Audit symbol metadata, memory accesses and call-state preservation separately.','Describe the CFA after every stack adjustment; return-value tests cannot validate the unwind description.'),
'T08.08':('Treat the operand list as the compiler\'s entire effect description.','An output written before a later input is consumed may need early-clobber even when one observed allocation works.'),
'T08.09':('Identify who constructs and restores the saved state at each transition.','A normal C call frame, kernel exception frame and language continuation have different invariants.'),
'T08.10':('Write the arithmetic precondition before comparing source and machine code.','Unsigned modulo arithmetic and signed overflow permit different optimizer arguments.'),
'T09.01':('Validate file extents before interpreting table entries.','Program headers describe loading; section tables describe link organization and may not be needed by a loader.'),
'T09.02':('Maintain a ledger of binding, definition and owning object.','Check whether an archive member was extracted before deciding which definition should win.'),
'T09.03':('Track unresolved names at the instant each archive is examined.','Separate forcing a member into the link from keeping one of its sections after extraction.'),
'T09.04':('State S, A, P, field width and signedness before encoding.','Check the mathematical range before reducing the value to its stored low bits.'),
'T09.05':('Separate executable role, position independence and runtime linkage.','Inspect actual final relocations and symbol binding after relaxation, not just compile flags.'),
'T09.06':('Record both the selected object and the scope used to find symbols.','Lazy function binding does not imply delayed variable relocation or missing recursive dependencies.'),
'T09.07':('Identify the producer of metadata and the code that consumes it.','Presence of an init array or TLS template does not establish that a particular instance was initialized.'),
'T09.08':('Keep VMA, LMA and file offset in separate columns.','Linker symbol values and stored C objects need different declaration and access conventions.'),
'T09.09':('Find the first stage where the registration entry disappears.','Compiler emission, archive extraction, section retention and runtime enumeration are separate gates.'),
'T09.10':('Decide whether the budget concerns file, load or runtime bytes.','Include alignment/reserved regions and distinguish initialized-data load copies from BSS residency.'),
'T09.11':('List names, layout, ownership and behavior as separate compatibility promises.','A symbol version can exist while violating the behavior promised to that version\'s callers.'),
'T09.12':('State address/base/gap-fill and checksum coverage before converting bytes.','Patching changes artifact identity; preserve the original debug association and verify the new image separately.'),
'T10.01':('Locate the first executed instruction rather than assuming it is main.','Preserve initial rsp before creating an ordinary C helper call frame.'),
'T10.02':('Draw pointer tables and pointed-to strings as separate regions.','Validate terminators/counts inside the supplied span before converting synthetic addresses into map lookups.'),
'T10.03':('Use the actual driver command to find installed startup objects.','Attribute each role through symbols/code; familiar source filenames do not establish a standardized interface.'),
'T10.04':('For each retained service identify the initializer it assumes.','The inspected musl sequence initializes TLS/stack protection before application code; a glibc entry-prefix reading is narrower.'),
'T10.05':('Separate userspace buffering/handlers from kernel process termination.','A custom entry has no ordinary caller return address; its bridge must own a no-return finish path.'),
'T10.06':('Draw C argument registers and syscall argument registers side by side.','Check argument4 and the instruction\'s rcx/r11 effects before diagnosing the higher-level transfer loop.'),
'T10.07':('Maintain an accepted prefix and unaccepted suffix.','An interrupted call without progress retains the same offset; a later error cannot undo already accepted bytes.'),
'T10.08':('Inspect final metadata and linked origins even when nm -u is empty.','Static resolution can hide a forbidden dependency, while static PIE can retain self-relocation work.'),
'T10.09':('Bound decimal magnitude and output extent before adding formatting.','Check overflow before multiplying by10 or adding a digit; compare binary dependencies after each increment.'),
'T10.10':('Break at the earliest entry handoff and retain the original machine state.','A reduction is valid only if it preserves the same violated invariant, not merely a nonzero exit.'),
'T11.01':('Draw the component boundary independently from the host verification process.','Classify source declarations, emitted helpers, transitive callbacks and OS services separately.'),
'T11.02':('Place each option in its compile, link or header-search stage.','A freestanding lowering may still emit byte helpers even when startup/default libraries are excluded.'),
'T11.03':('Inspect generated calls rather than searching only source call expressions.','Audit both object and final LTO output, including whether a byte provider accidentally calls itself.'),
'T11.04':('State the local arithmetic contract before matching a compiler helper name.','In long division retain the bit shifted above the fixed-width remainder before comparing/subtracting.'),
'T11.05':('Atomic correctness, lock freedom and instrumentation support are distinct claims.','Check actual effective flags and support symbols before labeling a build instrumented or production-independent.'),
'T11.06':('Derive movement from a snapshot of source bytes.','Choose direction using a justified address/arena model; ISO pointer ordering is not universal across unrelated objects.'),
'T11.07':('Enumerate the environment services the proposed library really calls.','A refusing backend must preserve state and expose unsupported work instead of fabricating successful progress.'),
'T11.08':('Assign one initialization owner to every retained runtime service.','Validate ranges and initialization order before letting hooks or tasks observe the state.'),
'T11.09':('Separate unresolved dependencies from already linked implementation origins.','A missing/truncated report cannot be interpreted as an empty allowlist violation set.'),
'T11.10':('Keep oracle computation outside the restricted target closure.','Enumerate valid arena partitions and minimize disagreements before broadening target claims.'),
}
ASSESSOR={
'T08.03.b':'For the declared integer pair, require RAX/RDX classification; for the triple require caller storage passed in RDI and the same address returned in RAX. A cast-based incompatible call is not a valid experiment. Mixed SSE/INTEGER return classification is the withheld changed condition.',
'T09.04.c':'The two values encode the same low byte EC but only -20 is in [-128,127]. A decoder that accepts236 after truncation erases the very overflow being assessed; a wider intermediate or independent integer arithmetic must precede encoding.',
'T09.09.a':'Ask for the archive member list before inspecting GC output. If the registration member never entered the link, KEEP has no matching input section. Targeted -u/extraction and KEEP solve different predicates; whole-archive is not a minimal explanation.',
'T10.02.a':'The synthetic word table occupies12 eightbytes. argc=2 gives argv at8 and null at24; one env pointer at32 and null at40 gives auxv at48. Termination occupies a type/value pair. Dereferencing8192 as a host pointer is a category error.',
'T10.07.a':'The successive submitted suffixes are ABCDEFG, CDEFG, CDEFG, FG. Total accepted progress is2+3+2. A mock accepting an impossible count must be rejected; min(count,remaining) would conceal a violated backend contract.',
'T11.04.c':'Maintain0<=r<d at the loop boundary. Shift/add may require129 bits; carry records that missing high bit. If carry is set the mathematical shifted remainder is at least2^128 and hence >=d. Subtraction modulo2^128 yields the representable reduced remainder because the mathematical result is<d.',
'T11.06.b':'The existing assessor uses uintptr_t ordering, which is appropriate only under its declared flat-address implementation assumptions. Within a single arena, offsets provide an alternative derivation; across unrelated objects an ISO relational pointer comparison is not a portable replacement.',
'T11.09.a':'A final fully linked original object can contain forbidden_helper while nm -u is empty and no DT_NEEDED exists. The new control therefore needs map/origin evidence; merely replaying the existing unresolved-object negative case does not assess this leaf extension.',
}
